6045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434053 #edb/ref 1077 "field-2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434053 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186434008 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434053 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "f09a48b6-6147-5c33-8f73-ea1439dfbd04" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434054 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186434045 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434054 #edb/ref 1069 "q-333068" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434054 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434054 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=3{x}_{1}(t)-{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=2{x}_{2}(t)+5,\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform $L$ to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a system with variables ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}.$ In terms of the parameter $s,$ the solution of the new system is\n\n${X}_{1}(s)=$ {{field-1}} $,\\,$\n${X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{s+5}{s(s-2)}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434054 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1151a388-649e-5c91-8e65-af0ed8268c10" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434054 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we compute the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}L\\{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{3{x}_{1}(t)-{x}_{2}(t)\\} \\\\ L\\{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{2{x}_{2}(t)+5\\}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}sL\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-{x}_{1}(0)=3L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\} \\\\ sL\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}-{x}_{2}(0)=2L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}+5L\\{1\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich can be simplified to the following:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-2=3{X}_{1}(s)-{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)-1=2{X}_{2}(s)+\\frac{5}{s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\},$ and we have used the fact that $L\\{1\\}=\\frac{1}{s}.$\n\nNow, solving the second equation for ${X}_{2}(s),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{2}(s)-1 & =2{X}_{2}(s)+\\frac{5}{s} \\\\ (s-2){X}_{2}(s) & =1+\\frac{5}{s} \\\\ (s-2){X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{s+5}{s} \\\\ {X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{s+5}{s(s-2)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this in the first equation and solving for ${X}_{1}(s)$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-2 & =3{X}_{1}(s)-{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ (s-3){X}_{1}(s) & =2-{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ (s-3){X}_{1}(s) & =2-(\\frac{s+5}{s(s-2)}) \\\\ (s-3){X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{2s(s-2)-(s+5)}{s(s-2)} \\\\ (s-3){X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{2({s}^{2}-2s)-s-5}{s(s-2)} \\\\ (s-3){X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{2{s}^{2}-4s-s-5}{s(s-2)} \\\\ (s-3){X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{2{s}^{2}-5s-5}{s(s-2)} \\\\ {X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{2{s}^{2}-5s-5}{s(s-2)(s-3)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution of the new system in terms of parameter $s$ is \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{2{s}^{2}-5s-5}{s(s-2)(s-3)},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{s+5}{s(s-2)}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434055 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186434036 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434055 #edb/ref 1069 "q-333061" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434055 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434055 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=-2{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=3{x}_{1}(t)+4{x}_{2}(t)+5,\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform $L$ to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a system with variables ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}.$ In terms of the parameter $s,$ the solution of the new system is\n\n${X}_{1}(s)=-\\frac{3}{s+2},\\,$\n${X}_{2}(s)=$ {{field-1}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434055 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4e326d04-8454-5a4c-8291-8ce0cd1c8852" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434055 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we compute the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}L\\{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{-2{x}_{1}(t)\\} \\\\ L\\{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{3{x}_{1}(t)+4{x}_{2}(t)+5\\}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}sL\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-{x}_{1}(0)=-2L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\} \\\\ sL\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}-{x}_{2}(0)=3L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}+4L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}+5L\\{1\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich can be simplified to the following:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)+3=-2{X}_{1}(s) \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)-1=3{X}_{1}(s)+4{X}_{2}(s)+\\frac{5}{s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\},$ and we have used the fact that $L\\{1\\}=\\frac{1}{s}.$\n\nNow, solving the first equation for ${X}_{1}(s),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)+3 & =-2{X}_{1}(s) \\\\ (s+2){X}_{1}(s) & =-3 \\\\ {X}_{1}(s) & =-\\frac{3}{s+2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this in the second equation and solving for ${X}_{2}(s),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{2}(s)-1 & =3{X}_{1}(s)+4{X}_{2}(s)+\\frac{5}{s} \\\\ (s-4){X}_{2}(s) & =3{X}_{1}(s)+\\frac{5}{s}+1 \\\\ (s-4){X}_{2}(s) & =3(-\\frac{3}{s+2})+\\frac{5+s}{s} \\\\ (s-4){X}_{2}(s) & =-\\frac{9}{s+2}+\\frac{5+s}{s} \\\\ (s-4){X}_{2}(s) & =-\\frac{9s}{s(s+2)}+\\frac{(5+s)(s+2)}{s(s+2)} \\\\ (s-4){X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{-9s+(5+s)(s+2)}{s(s+2)} \\\\ (s-4){X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{-9s+5s+{s}^{2}+10+2s}{s(s+2)} \\\\ {X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{{s}^{2}-2s+10}{s(s+2)(s-4)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution of the new system in terms of parameter $s$ is \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=-\\frac{3}{s+2},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{{s}^{2}-2s+10}{s(s+2)(s-4)}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434056 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186434032 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434056 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186434037 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434056 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186434041 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434056 #edb/ref 1069 "q-332815" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434056 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434056 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=3{x}_{1}(t)+{t}^{2}-4 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)={x}_{1}(t)+2{x}_{2}(t)+5,\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation, we get the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)+1={{field-1}}-\\frac{4}{s} \\\\ {{field-2}}={X}_{1}(s)+2{X}_{2}(s)+{{field-3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}$ are the Laplace transforms of the functions ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t),$ respectively." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434056 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "53078cf1-e2a6-5757-9214-0bb6642d4a23" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434056 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we compute the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}L\\{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{3{x}_{1}(t)+{t}^{2}-4\\} \\\\ L\\{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)+2{x}_{2}(t)+5\\}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}sL\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-{x}_{1}(0)=3L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}+L\\{{t}^{2}\\}-4L\\{1\\} \\\\ sL\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}-{x}_{2}(0)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}+2L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}+5L\\{1\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the results\n\n$$\nL\\{1\\}=\\frac{1}{s},\\,L\\{{t}^{2}\\}=\\frac{2}{{s}^{3}},\n$$\n\n we can write our system as follows:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)+1=3{X}_{1}(s)+\\frac{2}{{s}^{3}}-\\frac{4}{s} \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)-2={X}_{1}(s)+2{X}_{2}(s)+\\frac{5}{s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}$ are the Laplace transforms of the functions ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t),$ respectively." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434057 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186434038 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434057 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186434046 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434057 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186434052 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434057 #edb/ref 1069 "q-332822" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434057 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434057 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=2{x}_{1}(t)+2{e}^{-t} \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)={x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t)+3,\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation, we get the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{{field-1}}=2{X}_{1}(s)+{{field-2}} \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)+1={X}_{1}(s)+{X}_{2}(s)+{{field-3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}$ are the Laplace transforms of the functions ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t),$ respectively." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434057 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "66762fbf-e11e-5167-966c-39877463d24c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434057 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we compute the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}L\\{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{2{x}_{1}(t)+2{e}^{-t}\\} \\\\ L\\{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t)+3\\}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}sL\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-{x}_{1}(0)=2L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}+2L\\{{e}^{-t}\\} \\\\ sL\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}-{x}_{2}(0)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}+L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}+3L\\{1\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the results\n\n$$\nL\\{1\\}=\\frac{1}{s},\\,L\\{{e}^{-t}\\}=\\frac{1}{s+1},\n$$\n\nwe can write our system as follows:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)=2{X}_{1}(s)+\\frac{2}{s+1} \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)+1={X}_{1}(s)+{X}_{2}(s)+\\frac{3}{s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}$ are the Laplace transforms of the functions ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t),$ respectively." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434058 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186434042 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434058 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186434053 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434058 #edb/ref 1069 "q-333136" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434058 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434058 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=3{x}_{1}(t)-{x}_{2}(t)+4 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)={x}_{2}(t)-1,\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a transformed system with the solution \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}=\\frac{1}{s-1}+\\frac{1}{s-3}-\\frac{1}{s},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}=\\frac{2}{s-1}+\\frac{1}{s}.\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the original initial value problem.\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\" rowspan=\"2\">$x(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td height=\"35px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434058 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "69e91785-0e6d-5932-8b31-7b7666b19d7a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434058 #edb/ref 1074 "To find ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ satisfying the original initial value problem, we apply the inverse Laplace transform to ${X}_{1}(s)$ and ${X}_{2}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{1}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-1}+\\frac{1}{s-3}-\\frac{1}{s}\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-1}\\}+{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-3}\\}-{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s}\\} \\\\  & ={e}^{1\\cdot t}+{e}^{3\\cdot t}-1 \\\\  & ={e}^{t}+{e}^{3t}-1 \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{2}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{2}{s-1}+\\frac{1}{s}\\} \\\\  & =2\\,{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-1}\\}+{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s}\\} \\\\  & =2{e}^{1\\cdot t}+1 \\\\  & =2{e}^{t}+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3t}+{e}^{t}-1 \\\\ 2{e}^{t}+1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434059 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186434040 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434059 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186434047 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434059 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186434050 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434059 #edb/ref 1069 "q-332828" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434059 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434059 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=3{x}_{1}(t)+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-{x}_{1}(t)+2{x}_{2}(t)-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation, we get the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{{field-1}}={{field-2}} \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)=-{X}_{1}(s)+2{X}_{2}(s)-{{field-3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}$ are the Laplace transforms of the functions ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t),$ respectively." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434059 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "78263033-1bff-5da3-9201-fff7488d909f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434059 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we compute the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}L\\{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{3{x}_{1}(t)+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\} \\\\ L\\{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{-{x}_{1}(t)+2{x}_{2}(t)-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)\\}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}sL\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-{x}_{1}(0)=3L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}+4L\\{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\} \\\\ sL\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}-{x}_{2}(0)=-L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}+2L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}-3L\\{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the results\n\n$$\nL\\{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\}=\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+16},\\,L\\{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)\\}=\\frac{4}{{s}^{2}+16},\n$$\n\nwe can write our system as follows:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)=3{X}_{1}(s)+\\frac{4s}{{s}^{2}+16} \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)=-{X}_{1}(s)+2{X}_{2}(s)-\\frac{12}{{s}^{2}+16}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}$ are the Laplace transforms of the functions ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t),$ respectively." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434060 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186434035 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434060 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186434039 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434060 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186434049 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434060 #edb/ref 1069 "q-332827" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434060 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434060 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)={x}_{1}(t)-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-2{x}_{1}(t)+4{x}_{2}(t)+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation, we get the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-2={{field-1}} \\\\ {{field-2}}=-2{X}_{1}(s)+4{X}_{2}(s)+{{field-3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}$ are the Laplace transforms of the functions ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t),$ respectively." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434060 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7ee61787-7fd7-52ae-8d70-3b4f4209ed09" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434060 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we compute the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}L\\{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)\\} \\\\ L\\{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{-2{x}_{1}(t)+4{x}_{2}(t)+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}sL\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-{x}_{1}(0)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-5L\\{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)\\} \\\\ sL\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}-{x}_{2}(0)=-2L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}+4L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}+2L\\{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the results\n\n$$\nL\\{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)\\}=\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+1},\\,L\\{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)\\}=\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}+1},\n$$\n\nwe can write our system as follows:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-2={X}_{1}(s)-\\frac{5s}{{s}^{2}+1} \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)+1=-2{X}_{1}(s)+4{X}_{2}(s)+\\frac{2}{{s}^{2}+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}$ are the Laplace transforms of the functions ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t),$ respectively." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434061 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186434034 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434061 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186434051 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434061 #edb/ref 1069 "q-333124" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434061 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434061 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)={x}_{1}(t)+3 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-2{x}_{1}(t)+3{x}_{2}(t)-3,\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a transformed system with the solution \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}=\\frac{1}{s-1}-\\frac{3}{s},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}=\\frac{1}{s-1}-\\frac{1}{s}+\\frac{2}{s-3}.\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the original initial value problem.\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\" rowspan=\"2\">$x(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td height=\"35px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434061 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "80182570-5c16-548e-a977-c22b33e10f6d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434061 #edb/ref 1074 "To find ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ satisfying the original initial value problem, we apply the inverse Laplace transform to ${X}_{1}(s)$ and ${X}_{2}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{1}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-1}-\\frac{3}{s}\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-1}\\}-3{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s}\\} \\\\  & ={e}^{1\\cdot t}-3\\cdot 1 \\\\  & ={e}^{t}-3 \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{2}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-1}-\\frac{1}{s}+\\frac{2}{s-3}\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-1}\\}-{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s}\\}+2\\,{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-3}\\} \\\\  & ={e}^{1\\cdot t}-1+2{e}^{3\\cdot t} \\\\  & ={e}^{t}+2{e}^{3t}-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t}-3 \\\\ {e}^{t}+2{e}^{3t}-1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434062 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186434033 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434062 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186434048 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434062 #edb/ref 1069 "q-333129" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434062 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434062 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=3{x}_{1}(t)-3 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)={x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t)-3,\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a transformed system with the solution \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}=\\frac{2}{s-3}+\\frac{1}{s},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}=\\frac{1}{s-3}-\\frac{3}{s-1}+\\frac{2}{s}.\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the original initial value problem.\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\" rowspan=\"2\">$x(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td height=\"35px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434062 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "81e3b89d-a932-5551-882e-cf97243e80bc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434062 #edb/ref 1074 "To find ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ satisfying the original initial value problem, we apply the inverse Laplace transform to ${X}_{1}(s)$ and ${X}_{2}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{1}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{2}{s-3}+\\frac{1}{s}\\} \\\\  & =2\\,{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-3}\\}+{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s}\\} \\\\  & =2{e}^{3\\cdot t}+1 \\\\  & =2{e}^{3t}+1 \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{2}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-3}-\\frac{3}{s-1}+\\frac{2}{s}\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-3}\\}-3\\,{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-1}\\}+2\\,{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s}\\} \\\\  & ={e}^{3\\cdot t}-3{e}^{1\\cdot t}+2\\cdot 1 \\\\  & ={e}^{3t}-3{e}^{t}+2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{3t}+1 \\\\ {e}^{3t}-3{e}^{t}+2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434063 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186434043 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434063 #edb/ref 1069 "q-332785" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434063 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434063 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=3{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-2{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t)+3,\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform $L$ to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a system with variables ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}.$ In terms of the parameter $s,$ the solution of the new system is\n\n${X}_{1}(s)=-\\frac{1}{s-3},\\,$\n${X}_{2}(s)=$ {{field-1}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434063 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8dcb1599-ae92-594f-a29c-09dd73cb7136" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434063 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we compute the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}L\\{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{3{x}_{1}(t)\\} \\\\ L\\{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{-2{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t)+3\\}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}sL\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-{x}_{1}(0)=3L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\} \\\\ sL\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}-{x}_{2}(0)=-2L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}+L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}+3L\\{1\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich can be simplified to the following:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)+1=3{X}_{1}(s) \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)-2=-2{X}_{1}(s)+{X}_{2}(s)+\\frac{3}{s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\},$ and we have used the fact that $L\\{1\\}=\\frac{1}{s}.$\n\nNow, solving the first equation for ${X}_{1}(s),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)+1 & =3{X}_{1}(s) \\\\ (s-3){X}_{1}(s) & =-1 \\\\ {X}_{1}(s) & =-\\frac{1}{s-3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this in the second equation and solving for ${X}_{2}(s),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{2}(s)-2 & =-2{X}_{1}(s)+{X}_{2}(s)+\\frac{3}{s} \\\\ (s-1){X}_{2}(s) & =-2{X}_{1}(s)+2+\\frac{3}{s} \\\\ (s-1){X}_{2}(s) & =-2(-\\frac{1}{s-3})+2+\\frac{3}{s} \\\\ (s-1){X}_{2}(s) & =(\\frac{2}{s-3})+(\\frac{2s+3}{s}) \\\\ (s-1){X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{2s+(2s+3)(s-3)}{s(s-3)} \\\\ (s-1){X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{2s+(2{s}^{2}-3s-9)}{s(s-3)} \\\\ (s-1){X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{2{s}^{2}-s-9}{s(s-3)} \\\\ {X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{2{s}^{2}-s-9}{s(s-1)(s-3)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution of the new system in terms of parameter $s$ is \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=-\\frac{1}{s-3},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{2{s}^{2}-s-9}{s(s-1)(s-3)}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434064 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186434044 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434064 #edb/ref 1069 "q-333055" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434064 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434064 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=3{x}_{1}(t)-2 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=2{x}_{1}(t)+5{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform $L$ to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a system with variables ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}.$ In terms of the parameter $s,$ the solution of the new system is\n\n${X}_{1}(s)=-\\frac{s+2}{s(s-3)},\\,$\n${X}_{2}(s)=$ {{field-1}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434064 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b4ba1928-c543-554d-8f81-96f348be498a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434064 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we compute the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}L\\{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{3{x}_{1}(t)-2\\} \\\\ L\\{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{2{x}_{1}(t)+5{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}sL\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-{x}_{1}(0)=3L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-2L\\{1\\} \\\\ sL\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}-{x}_{2}(0)=2L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}+5L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich can be simplified to the following:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)+1=3{X}_{1}(s)-\\frac{2}{s} \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)-4=2{X}_{1}(s)+5{X}_{2}(s)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\},$ and we have used the fact that $L\\{1\\}=\\frac{1}{s}.$\n\nNow, solving the first equation for ${X}_{1}(s),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)+1 & =3{X}_{1}(s)-\\frac{2}{s} \\\\ (s-3){X}_{1}(s) & =-1-\\frac{2}{s} \\\\ (s-3){X}_{1}(s) & =-(1+\\frac{2}{s}) \\\\ (s-3){X}_{1}(s) & =-(\\frac{s+2}{s}) \\\\ {X}_{1}(s) & =-\\frac{s+2}{s(s-3)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this in the second equation and solving for ${X}_{2}(s),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{2}(s)-4 & =2{X}_{1}(s)+5{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ (s-5){X}_{2}(s) & =2{X}_{1}(s)+4 \\\\ (s-5){X}_{2}(s) & =2(-\\frac{s+2}{s(s-3)})+4 \\\\ (s-5){X}_{2}(s) & =-\\frac{2(s+2)}{s(s-3)}+4 \\\\ (s-5){X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{-2(s+2)+4s(s-3)}{s(s-3)} \\\\ (s-5){X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{-2s-4+4{s}^{2}-12s}{s(s-3)} \\\\ (s-5){X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{4{s}^{2}-14s-4}{s(s-3)} \\\\ {X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{4{s}^{2}-14s-4}{s(s-3)(s-5)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution of the new system in terms of parameter $s$ is \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=-\\frac{s+2}{s(s-3)},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{4{s}^{2}-14s-4}{s(s-3)(s-5)}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
